---
import Layout from '../layouts/layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/footer.astro';
import ProseStyles from '../components/prose-styles.astro';

const LAST_UPDATED = '9 September 2026';
const SUPPORT_EMAIL = 'support@marginapp.in';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Use — Margin"
  description="The terms on which Yuktibyte Products Private Limited provides Margin, the personal investment cockpit for Indian equity investors."
>
  <Nav />
  <ProseStyles />

  <main class="pt-32 pb-24">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">

      <div class="reveal mb-12">
        <p class="text-xs text-gold-400 tracking-widest uppercase mb-4">Legal</p>
        <h1 class="font-display text-5xl md:text-6xl font-light text-cream leading-tight mb-6">
          Terms of <em class="font-semibold not-italic">Use</em>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-muted text-lg leading-relaxed">
          These terms govern your use of Margin and of the marginapp.in websites. Please read them
          before you create an account. By signing up or using the service, you agree to them.
        </p>
        <p class="text-xs text-muted/70 tracking-widest uppercase mt-6">Last updated {LAST_UPDATED}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-navy-800/30 border border-gold-400/30 rounded-xl p-6 mb-16 reveal reveal-delay-1">
        <p class="text-xs text-gold-400 tracking-widest uppercase mb-3">Read this first</p>
        <p class="text-cream text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Margin is a record-keeping and analysis tool. It is not investment advice. Yuktibyte
          Products Private Limited is not registered with SEBI as an investment adviser, a research
          analyst, a portfolio manager or a stock broker, and nothing in the product or on these
          websites is a recommendation to buy, sell or hold any security. Every valuation, expected
          return and verdict you see is arithmetic run on assumptions that you chose. Your investment
          decisions, and their outcomes, are entirely your own.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose-margin reveal">

        <h2>1. Who you are contracting with</h2>
        <p>
          Margin is operated by Yuktibyte Products Private Limited, a company incorporated in India
          under CIN U62099KA2025PTC196482, with its registered office in Bengaluru, Karnataka. In
          these terms, "we", "us" and "our" mean Yuktibyte Products Private Limited, and "you" means
          the person using the service. Our company details are listed on the
          <a href="/company">Company</a> page.
        </p>
        <p>
          "Margin" or "the service" means the application at go.marginapp.in, the websites at
          marginapp.in, the research library, the Screen tool, the API, and any related content we
          publish, including guides, insights and stock and industry story videos.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Accepting these terms</h2>
        <p>
          You accept these terms when you create an account or otherwise use the service. If you are
          using Margin on behalf of a company, a partnership or a trust, you confirm that you are
          authorised to bind that entity, and these terms then apply to it. If you do not agree with
          any part of these terms, please do not use Margin.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Eligibility and your account</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>You must be at least 18 years old and legally able to enter into a contract under Indian law.</li>
          <li>You agree to give accurate account information and to keep it current.</li>
          <li>You are responsible for everything done through your account, including anything done with an API token you created.</li>
          <li>You must keep your login credentials and API tokens confidential, and tell us promptly if you believe either has been compromised.</li>
          <li>An account is for one person. Please do not share your login with others or create accounts on behalf of people who have not asked you to.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. What Margin does, and what it does not do</h2>
        <p>
          Margin holds your holdings and trades, your dividends, your funds statement, your DCF and
          reverse DCF valuations, your price anchors, your target allocation, your lists, tags and
          notes, and it computes returns, capital gains and tax figures from them. It is a cockpit
          for information you supply and assumptions you set.
        </p>
        <p>Margin does not do the following, and you should not rely on it as though it did:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>It does not give investment, legal, accounting or tax advice, and it does not consider your financial position, risk appetite or objectives.</li>
          <li>It does not execute, route or place trades, and it holds no client funds or securities.</li>
          <li>It is not a substitute for your broker's contract notes, your demat statement, or the filings and disclosures a company makes.</li>
          <li>It is not a substitute for a chartered accountant. Capital gains and tax figures are computed from the trades and rates available to us, and they are an aid to your own filing rather than a return you can file as it stands.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          You are responsible for verifying anything you act on. Where a number matters to a decision
          or to a filing, check it against your broker, your depository or your own records.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Your data and the files you upload</h2>
        <p>
          Your portfolio data stays yours. You keep all rights in the holdings, tradebooks, dividend
          records, funds statements, valuations, notes, tags and lists you put into Margin. You grant
          us a limited licence to store and process that content for the sole purpose of operating
          the service for you, including computing valuations and returns, and supporting you when
          you ask for help.
        </p>
        <p>
          You confirm that you have the right to upload what you upload. Please do not put another
          person's portfolio, personal details or broker statements into Margin unless that person
          has authorised you to do so.
        </p>
        <p>
          How we handle personal data, and the way the funds statement in particular is read in your
          browser and hashed on arrival, is described in our
          <a href="/#privacy">privacy summary</a> and in
          <a href="/privacy-vault">how Privacy Vault protects you</a>. Those pages are part of these
          terms by reference.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Market data, valuations and research</h2>
        <p>
          Prices in Margin come from the exchange bhavcopy at the close. They are end of day rather
          than live, and Margin shows you the date of the quote you are reading. Corporate actions,
          symbol changes and exchange revisions can take time to reflect, and data from any upstream
          source can be delayed, incomplete or wrong.
        </p>
        <p>
          A DCF, a reverse DCF, a forward projection, an expected return or a what-if price is a
          calculation over inputs you supply. Change an assumption and the answer changes. These
          outputs carry no forecast of any actual result, and past returns computed inside Margin say
          nothing about future ones.
        </p>
        <p>
          Research library reports, quick previews used in Screen, guides, insights and videos are
          published for information and education. They are prepared from public sources and from
          our own reading of a business, they can contain errors, they go out of date, and they are
          not tailored to you. A Yes, Maybe, No or Never you record in Screen is your own note to
          yourself and carries no view of ours.
        </p>

        <h2>7. API tokens and automated access</h2>
        <p>
          You may create personal API tokens so that an AI agent or a script of your own can work
          with your data, following the machine-readable instructions we publish. When you do:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>The token acts as you, and you are responsible for every call made with it, including calls made by an agent or a third-party tool you have connected.</li>
          <li>Please keep tokens secret. Do not commit them to a repository, paste them into a shared prompt, or hand them to a service you do not trust.</li>
          <li>You may revoke a token at any time, and we may revoke or rate-limit a token that is being used in a way that threatens the stability of the service or the security of other users.</li>
          <li>Uploads through the API replace or extend data as documented. You are responsible for understanding what a given call overwrites before you automate it.</li>
          <li>We may set and change rate limits, quotas and the shape of API endpoints. Automated clients should tolerate change.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>8. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>While using Margin, you agree not to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Resell, sublicense, redistribute or publicly republish the research library, Screen previews, guides or other content we produce, or use them to build a competing dataset or product.</li>
          <li>Scrape, crawl or bulk-extract content or data beyond what the API and the interface are meant to provide.</li>
          <li>Reverse engineer, decompile or attempt to derive the source of the service, except to the extent Indian law expressly permits.</li>
          <li>Probe, scan or test the security of the service, circumvent authentication or rate limits, or access data that is not yours.</li>
          <li>Upload malware, or content that is unlawful, infringing or that you have no right to share.</li>
          <li>Use the service in a way that degrades it for other users, or that breaches SEBI regulations, exchange rules, or any other applicable law.</li>
          <li>Present output from Margin to other people as regulated investment advice, or use it to run an advisory or research business without the registrations that business requires.</li>
        </ul>

