          in these terms is reserved.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may quote a short extract of our published writing with attribution and a link. Please
          ask us first for anything more.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you send us feedback, feature ideas or bug reports, we may use them freely to improve
          Margin, without obligation or payment to you.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Pricing and the free plan</h2>
        <p>
          Margin is currently offered on a free inaugural plan, with no card required. That plan is
          introductory and its terms will change. We may introduce paid plans, move features between
          plans, or set limits on usage. We will give you notice before a change starts to affect an
          existing account, and you will always have the choice to export your data and stop using
          the service instead of accepting a new price.
        </p>
        <p>
          Where charges do apply in future, they will be stated at the point of purchase along with
          taxes, billing period and any refund terms, and those stated terms will govern that
          purchase.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Availability and changes to the service</h2>
        <p>
          Margin is a young product under active development. We may add, change or remove features,
          adjust how a calculation is presented, or take the service down for maintenance. We do not
          promise any particular level of uptime, and we do not offer a service level agreement on
          the free plan. Where a change would remove something you depend on, we will try to give
          reasonable notice.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Suspension, termination and deletion</h2>
        <p>
          You may stop using Margin at any time and ask us to delete your account. On deletion, we
          remove your personal data from the vault and your portfolio records from our systems,
          except where we must retain something to meet a legal obligation, and except for backups
          that expire on their normal cycle.
        </p>
        <p>
          We may suspend or terminate an account that breaches these terms, that puts the security or
          stability of the service at risk, or where we are required to do so by law. Where the
          circumstances allow it, we will tell you why and give you a chance to put things right, and
          we will give you a reasonable window to export your data.
        </p>

        <h2>13. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
        <p>
          The service is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis. To the fullest extent
          permitted by law, we disclaim all warranties, express or implied, including any warranty of
          merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, non-infringement, and any warranty that
          the service will be uninterrupted, secure, error-free, or that data, prices, valuations,
          returns, capital gains or tax figures within it will be accurate, complete or current.
        </p>

        <h2>14. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any investment loss, trading
          loss, lost profit, lost opportunity, loss of data, or any indirect, incidental, special,
          consequential or punitive damages arising out of your use of Margin, whether the claim is
